This tells us the minimum value of $g(x)$ on the set
\[x \ge 8 = \{ x : x - 8 \ge 0, x \in \mathbb{R} \}.\]On the set
\[x < 8 = \{ x : x - 8 \le 0, x \in \mathbb{R} \},\]we get
\[g(x) = -\frac{x^2}{8 - x}.\]This is getting even closer and closer to $-x,$ which means the minimum value is not achieved.

On the set
\[8 < x < 16 = \{ x : x - 8 > 0, x - 16 < 0, x \in \mathbb{R} \},\]we get
\[g(x) = x + 8 + \frac{64}{x - 8} = x - 8 + \frac{64}{x - 8} + 16.\]The minimum value occurs when
\[x - 8 - \frac{64}{x - 8} = 0,\] or $x - 8 = 8,$ so $x = 16.$

On the set
\[x > 16 = \{ x : x - 16 \ge 0, x \in \mathbb{R} \},\]we have
\begin{align*}
g(x) &= x + \frac{x^2}{x - 16} \\
&= x + \frac{x^2 - 16x + 16x}{x - 16} \\
&= x + \frac{(x - 8)^2}{x - 16} + 16x \\
&\qquad = x + \frac{8(x - 8)}{x - 16} + 16x.
\end{align*}The minimum value occurs when
\[\frac{x - 8}{x - 16} = -\frac{1}{2}.\]This leads to $x - 16 = -(x - 8),$ so $x = 12.$

Therefore, the minimum value is $\boxed{16}.$ </think> <answer> 16 </answer>

