Since the corresponding angles in $\triangle WYX$ and $\triangle WZX$ are equal (since $\angle XYZ$ is an alternate interior angle between $\overline{ZX}$ and $WY$, both of which are tangent to the same circle), the two triangles will be similar, making $AX=\frac{WY}{3}WZ=4WZ=48$ and $XY=WY-AX=2WY=36$ since $\triangle WYX$ will always be a $4-3-5$ right triangle (which is also a little famous right triangle): [asy]
